<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 29,648 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 29,648 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 29,648 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 95,897 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,043	    7,196</p>
<p>    Import cargo			18,605	   88,701</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and 12 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    52,000	 Keefan		4/10</p>
<p>Jute			5,419	 Al-Salma	     due</p>
<p>High speed deisel    34,000	 Al-Deerah	   2/11</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Gemstar-1	    due</p>
<p>Fertilizer	     31,802	 Cargo Explorer    1/11</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Crystal River     3/11</p>
<p>Pig Iron		  4,984	 Trunovsk	     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
